text.en:
Powers and Functions. The OPS shall perform the following
a. Discharge the function of speaking for the President on matters pertaining to
his actions, policies, programs, official activities and accomplishments;
b. Coordinate and cultivate relations with private mass media entities;
c. Provide news and information to the public by utilizing relevant mass media
and other emerging platforms;
d. Develop and implement necessary guidelines and mechanisms pertaining to
the dissemination of information on the policies, programs, official activities
and achievements of the President;
e. Provide a mechanism to address special concerns of the OP for better
communication with the Filipino people as well as with foreign media;
f. Submit periodic reports to the President, through the Executive Secretary, on
the status of programs and projects undertaken; and
g. Perform such other functions as the President may direct.
The OPS and PCOO shall coordinate on all activities when the nature thereof
is directly relevant to the functions of both.
